        {
          "check": "party_blind",
          "severity": "warning",
          "detail": "The rationale states the structural inequality is 'built into the visa system by design', which edges toward motive attribution. The policy text does explicitly create health-status-based differential charging, so the structural observation is valid \u2014 but 'by design' implies deliberate discriminatory intent rather than simply describing the modelled effect. Recommend replacing with neutral descriptive language such as 'as an explicit feature of the policy mechanism'."
        }
      ],
      "notes": "The core O9 verdict \u2014 that health-status-contingent variable charging differentiates migrants by a protected characteristic (disability/health condition under the Equality Act 2010) \u2014 is well-grounded in the stated policy text and is legitimate scope for O9. The direction ('worsens') and magnitude ('moderate') are supported by the surviving claims. No blocking issues found; three warnings should be addressed before publication."
